WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.053
<v Examiner>Myopia, hyperopia and astigmatism.

2
00:00:04.053 --> 00:00:04.909
<v Examiner>Five marks.

3
00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:11.403
<v Examiner>Explain how myopia, emmetropia and hyperopia differ, and how each error is corrected.

4
00:00:11.403 --> 00:00:12.825
<v Examiner>What is astigmatism?

5
00:00:13.275 --> 00:00:15.869
The hook: myopia, my world is up close.

6
00:00:15.869 --> 00:00:16.800
Short-sighted.

7
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.188
The focus falls short, in front of the retina, and a concave lens pushes it back.

8
00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:27.974
Hyperopia: the focus overshoots, behind the retina, and a convex lens pulls it forward.

9
00:00:28.424 --> 00:00:30.321
Emmetropia is normal vision.

10
00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:33.437
Parallel light rays are focused on the retina.

11
00:00:33.887 --> 00:00:35.639
Myopia is short-sightedness.

12
00:00:35.639 --> 00:00:39.267
Light from distant objects focuses in front of the retina,

13
00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:41.770
usually because the eyeball is too long.

14
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.898
Near things are clear, and far things are blurred.

15
00:00:44.898 --> 00:00:49.840
It's corrected with a concave lens, which diverges the light, spreading it out,

16
00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.405
and moves the focus back onto the retina.

17
00:00:53.855 --> 00:00:55.758
Hyperopia is long-sightedness.

18
00:00:55.758 --> 00:00:58.929
Light from near objects focuses behind the retina,

19
00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:01.530
usually because the eyeball is too short.

20
00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.940
Far things are clearer than near ones.

21
00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.097
It's corrected with a convex lens,

22
00:01:06.097 --> 00:01:10.537
which converges the light and moves the focus forward onto the retina.

23
00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:14.758
Astigmatism: the cornea or the lens is curved unevenly,

24
00:01:14.758 --> 00:01:17.158
more in one direction than another.

25
00:01:17.158 --> 00:01:22.299
So light focuses at several points, and vision is blurred at all distances.

26
00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:27.030
It's corrected with glasses or contact lenses, or with laser surgery.

27
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.142
The traps.

28
00:01:29.142 --> 00:01:31.194
Myopia: short-sighted, concave.

29
00:01:31.194 --> 00:01:33.313
Hyperopia: long-sighted, convex.

30
00:01:33.313 --> 00:01:36.094
Swapping the lenses is the commonest slip.

31
00:01:36.094 --> 00:01:40.596
Second: say where the image falls, in front of or behind the retina.

32
00:01:40.596 --> 00:01:42.913
That's the mark, not just "blurry".

33
00:01:42.913 --> 00:01:45.959
Third: astigmatism doesn't depend on distance.

34
00:01:45.959 --> 00:01:47.680
It's blurred near and far.

35
00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:48.838
<v Examiner>Once more.

36
00:01:48.838 --> 00:01:51.245
<v Examiner>Myopia, hyperopia and astigmatism.

37
00:01:53.695 --> 00:01:56.340
Emmetropia: light is focused on the retina.

38
00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:01.693
Myopia, short-sighted: distant light focuses in front of the retina because the eyeball

39
00:02:01.693 --> 00:02:04.831
is too long, and a concave lens diverges the light.

40
00:02:04.831 --> 00:02:06.308
Hyperopia, long-sighted:

41
00:02:06.308 --> 00:02:10.615
near light focuses behind the retina because the eyeball is too short,

42
00:02:10.615 --> 00:02:12.953
and a convex lens converges the light.

43
00:02:12.953 --> 00:02:16.091
Astigmatism: the cornea or lens is curved unevenly,

44
00:02:16.091 --> 00:02:19.845
so light focuses at several points and everything is blurred.

45
00:02:19.845 --> 00:02:22.060
Glasses, contacts, or laser surgery.
